				<h1>How To (Use The Platform)</h1>
				<h2>How to get started using iDAL as your booking platform</h2>
				<p>Yey! You’re in! First of all, a big welcome to you, we are thrilled to have you onboard. Now that you have created your basic profile with username (email) and password, let’s try to get you verified as a pro as soon as possible so that our clients can find your gorgeous self. Follow the simple steps below and we will notify you within a few days to let you know if you have been approved and can start receiving job offers. How exciting!</p>
				
				<h3>1. Edit Profile</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Have your measurement tape ready! Fill in all necessary measurements of your body and dressing sizes so that clients can check if you are right for their products.</li>
					<li>ID please! Upload a copy of your ID, it can either be a snapshot of your passport or a drivers licence. Make sure the passport snap includes the passport number and the expiration date. Pst! This is essential to get verified.</li> 
					<li>Then add your matching date of birth, place and nationality in your profile (don’t worry, it is not visible to any clients).</li>
					<li>What’s your Insta? Link your @instagram account.</li>
					<li>Share your experience! For a client it is also essential that they can see what type of jobs you have done recently. Head to the experience section next to write down your most relevant past modeling jobs.</li>
				</ul>
				
				<h3>2. Edit Portfolio</h3>
				<ul>
				<li>Time to show off your coolest photos! Upload your high resolution portfolio photos from work and tests. The first photo will be on your digital composite card, so make sure it is a stunning headshot to impress them. </li>
				<li>In addition to your headshot, you need to upload at least 5 additional photos so that clients can see your work. But if you are able, we'd prefer you upload as many as 12-14, and certainly no less than 8-10 high quality pics. Make sure to include 2-3 full length, 1-2 close ups, 2-3 in lingerie/swimwear if that applies to you, your editorial jobs and advertising campaigns if you have done any, etc. We believe you know which pictures represent you best so have fun picking them!</li>
				<li>Want to know how to put together a portfolio like a pro? <a href="/howto#martine">Check this out</a>.</li>
				</ul>
				
				<h3>3. Edit Polaroids</h3>
				<ul>
				<li>Hello natural beauty! Please upload your most recent polaroids here. 4 polaroids (digitals) are required. In case you do Lingerie and Swimwear jobs, please upload at least 2 additional polas wearing lingerie/swimwear. </li>
				<li>Pay attention to the first polaroid, it will become your profile photo! This photo will show up in search results for clients before they click on your profile, so make it a stunning natural headshot. You can click on the check mark on the photo you would like to choose for this.</li>
				<li>NB! Check out our guide on how to take <a href="/howto#martine">amazing polaroids here</a>.</li>
				</ul>
				
				<h3>4. Edit availability
				<ul>
					<li>Off duty? Please let us know if you are currently not available for jobs, and clients won’t be able to find you in the search results when looking for models to book.</li>
				</ul>
				
				<h3>5. Payments</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Let’s get down to business! Insert your average rate that you are comfortable with accepting. This is personal, so it is up to you how low or high you want to set your minimum. Note that clients with lower budgets than your set limit won’t see you in their search result. Also it is good to remember that you are always free to Accept or Decline option requests, and this can also be changed at any time.</li>
					<li>Pay day! Add your bank account details so you are able to receive direct payment for the jobs you have done.</li>
				</ul> 
								
